{"seq":2,"slug":"elbo","title":"ELBO：变分推断的唯一目标函数","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/variational-inference/elbo","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"elbo-derivation","title":"ELBO 推导：证据、下界与那道恒等式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/variational-inference/elbo/elbo-derivation","wordCount":1477,"readingTime":6},{"seq":2,"slug":"kl-divergence","title":"KL 散度与方向：为什么变分近似总是过度自信","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/variational-inference/elbo/kl-divergence","wordCount":1527,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"elbo-decomposition","title":"ELBO 分解与解读：重构、正则与自由能","url":"/l-doc-books/h/data-science/variational-inference/elbo/elbo-decomposition","wordCount":1579,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"elbo-变分推断的唯一目标函数\">ELBO：变分推断的唯一目标函数</h1><p>如果说基础章回答了「为什么把推断变成优化」，那么这一章回答的是「优化的到底是哪个函数」。答案只有一个名字：证据下界（Evidence Lower Bound, ELBO）。变分推断所有的算法差异，都只是在用不同方式最大化同一个 ELBO，所以这一章是整个 hub 的数学心脏。</p>\n<p>第一篇《ELBO 推导》给出它的来历。从对数证据 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\log p(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 出发，用一条恒等式 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∥</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\log p(x) = \\mathrm{ELBO}(q) + \\mathrm{KL}(q\\,\\|\\,p(z\\mid x))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ELBO</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">KL</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span></span> 把证据、下界与「近似分布离真后验有多远」三者串起来；再用 Jensen 不等式给出第二条独立的推导路径。关键结论：因为 KL 非负，ELBO 永远是 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\log p(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 的下界，而抬高下界就等于压低 KL——于是「逼近后验」和「最大化 ELBO」是同一件事。</p>\n<p>第二篇《KL 散度与方向》盯住那个 KL 项深挖。KL 不对称，VI 用的是反向 KL <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∥</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{KL}(q\\|p)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">KL</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mord\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 而非正向 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∥</mi><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{KL}(p\\|q)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">KL</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mord\">∥</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span>，这个选择不是随意的，它直接决定了变分近似「抓单个模式、系统性低估方差」的著名脾气。这一篇讲清两个方向的几何差异（mode-seeking 对 mean-seeking），以及它对下游不确定性估计的实际影响。</p>\n<p>第三篇《ELBO 分解与解读》把 ELBO 拆成人能读懂的部件：一项是「重构」——数据在近似后验下的期望对数似然；一项是「正则」——近似后验对先验的 KL。这正是 VAE 损失里那两项的来源，也解释了 VI 与统计物理里「变分自由能」的对应。</p>\n<p>三篇读完，你会把 ELBO 看成一个可以从三个不同角度审视的同一对象，为算法章的各种最大化手段做好准备。</p>\n"}